From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:20:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: apple,pmgr-pwrstate: Add
 apple,sleep-retained

A coprocessor can keep running in its power domain across system sleep
without system-sleep callbacks of its own, as the J713's GPU firmware
does. Describe such a domain, which the OS keeps on during system
sleep; runtime power management is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 7c714f5f145f09e55769c11f2deb3a1dcb355491)
[dylan: without the T8132 apple,inherited-on if/then block of the
 original's context, which this tree's binding does not have.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml     | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml
index 7800f0f106..22e7735441 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml
@@ -89,6 +89,13 @@ properties:
       coprocessors' CPU domains.
     type: boolean
 
+  apple,sleep-retained:
+    description:
+      A coprocessor keeps running in this domain across system sleep with no
+      system-sleep callbacks of its own. The OS keeps the domain on during
+      system sleep. Runtime power management is unaffected.
+    type: boolean
+
